  "summary": "pylever exfiltrates Discord tokens from installer workspace to hardcoded webhook on import",
  "details": "On `import pylever`, __init__.py imports token_saver which unconditionally instantiates _Client() and calls auto_save_tokens() at module top level. _TokenFinder.find_all() recursively rglob's the current working directory, applies the Discord bot-token regex `[MN][A-Za-z0-9_-]{71}` to every non-skipped file, and _Client.auto_save_tokens posts each match to the hardcoded webhook `https://discord.com/api/webhooks/1542822306194259988/...` via send_token_to_discord. The webhook URL is baked into the shipped code with no caller-configurable override. Any Discord bot token present in the installer's source tree,.env files, or other workspace files is captured and transmitted to the author. setup.py ships placeholder author metadata (`Your Name`, `your.email@example.com`, `github.com/yourusername/pylever`). The README's 'token saver' framing does not constitute consent for whole-workspace credential harvesting to a fixed third-party endpoint.",
